<h2>Why pay when the calendar is free?</h2>
<p>The calendar is the record. Alerts is the watch. Counties post a date, move it, pull properties and close registration well before the sale, and none of them email you. Lake County, Illinois, for example, closed registration on Oct 23, 2026 for a sale three weeks later. Alerts puts those deadlines at the top of every email.</p>

<h2>What's in each weekly email</h2>
<dl class="facts">
  <dt>When</dt><dd>Once a week, after our weekly check of every county source page.</dd>
  <dt>Deadlines</dt><dd>Every registration deadline in the next 30 days, soonest first, with the sale it's for. If a county's own pages disagree on a deadline, we say so and give the earlier one.</dd>
  <dt>Coming up</dt><dd>Every dated sale in the next 30 days, grouped by state, with date, time, online or in person, deposit and a link to the county page it came from.</dd>
  <dt>What changed</dt><dd>Sales a county added, moved or cancelled since the last email.</dd>
  <dt>Parcel lists</dt><dd>When a county publishes the list of properties in its sale and its terms allow reuse, we send it as a spreadsheet. Some counties allow personal use only or forbid copying, and private auction platforms keep their own lists. For those we link straight to the county or platform.</dd>
  <dt>Coverage</dt><dd>{{ counties.length }} counties and towns in {% for st in states %}{{ st.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. We add more every month, starting with the ones subscribers ask for.</dd>
</dl>

